re grid: $\\overrightarrow{OA}=\\mathbf{a}$, $\\overrightarrow{OB}=\\mathbf{b}$, and $\\overrightarrow{OC}=\\mathbf{c}$.\n\n![Vector diagram](images/a7/a7c8651a67d96846172792412818a0b3dca3b473ec064abbfc6a5ddc304be19e.png)\n\nGiven that $\\mathbf{c}=\\lambda\\mathbf{a}+\\mu\\mathbf{b}$, find $\\lambda$ and $\\mu$.\n\n$\\lambda=$ {{field-1}}\n\n$\\mu=$ {{field-2}}"] [:db/add "24ebf79a-17a7-5d88-a3c9-9ccc5e4ec0c8" :question/worked-solution "![Completed vector route](images/16/16e49d3f1ffc9798f206c2fd6e956589f884075bb984fb9a5cf8aa8a8f5addb5.png)\n\nConstruct the route $O\\to X\\to C$, first parallel to $\\mathbf{b}$ and then parallel to $\\mathbf{a}$.\n\nAlong $OX$, move $2$ squares left. A copy of $\\mathbf{b}$ moves $1$ square left. Thus $OX=2|\\mathbf{b}|$ and the segment points in the same direction to $\\mathbf{b}$. Hence $\\overrightarrow{OX}=2\\mathbf{b}$.\n\nAlong $XC$, move $2$ squares left and $2$ squares down. A copy of $\\mathbf{a}$ moves $1$ square left and $1$ square down. Thus $XC=2|\\mathbf{a}|$ and the segment points in the same direction to $\\mathbf{a}$. Hence $\\overrightarrow{XC}=2\\mathbf{a}$.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathbf{c}&=\\overrightarrow{OX}+\\overrightarrow{XC}\\\\&=2\\mathbf{b}+2\\mathbf{a}\\\\&=2\\mathbf{a}+2\\mathbf{b}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nReorder the terms to match their vector names. Since $\\mathbf{a}$ and $\\mathbf{b}$ are not parallel, their coefficients are unique. Matching coefficients gives $\\lambda=2$ and $\\mu=2$."] [:db/add "24ebf79a-17a7-5d88-a3c9-9ccc5e4ec0c8" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy] [:db/add "24ebf79a-17a7-5d88-a3c9-9ccc5e4ec0c8" :question/answer-fields "642c77d9-6474-5691-97f8-eca7e1d8a566"] [:db/add "24ebf79a-17a7-5d88-a3c9-9ccc5e4ec0c8" :question/answer-fields "8a69d291-b8ea-5f04-b93a-89e30dfe8113"] [:db/ensure "24ebf79a-17a7-5d88-a3c9-9ccc5e4ec0c8" :question/validate] [:db/add 17592186096652 :knowledge-point/questions "24ebf79a-17a7-5d88-a3c9-9ccc5e4ec0c8"] [:db/add "ca9a3680-3a2a-52d1-b76e-e5573c9f5f49" :answer/id #uuid "ca9a3680-3a2a-52d1-b76e-e5573c9f5f49"] [:db/add "ca9a3680-3a2a-52d1-b76e-e5573c9f5f49" :answer/type :answer.type/math] [:db/add "ca9a3680-3a2a-52d1-b76e-e5573c9f5f49" :answer/value "2"] [:db/ensure "ca9a3680-3a2a-52d1-b76e-e5573c9f5f49" :answer/validate] [:db/add "e1801d11-b878-56a6-a349-2f7b86d97789" :answer-field/id #uuid "e1801d11-b878-56a6-a349-2f7b86d97789"] [:db/add "e1801d11-b878-56a6-a349-2f7b86d97789" :answer-field/key "field-1"] [:db/add "e1801d11-b878-56a6-a349-2f7b86d97789" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank] [:db/add "e1801d11-b878-56a6-a349-2f7b86d97789" :answer-field/choices "ca9a3680-3a2a-52d1-b76e-e5573c9f5f49"] [:db/add "e1801d11-b878-56a6-a349-2f7b86d97789" :answer-field/correct "ca9a3680-3a2a-52d1-b76e-e5573c9f5f49"] [:db/ensure "e1801d11-b878-56a6-a349-2f7b86d97789" :answer-field/validate] [:db/add "9610abe5-88c2-5a6a-9548-130464947fbb" :answer/id #uuid "9610abe5-88c2-5a6a-9548-130464947fbb"] [:db/add "9610abe5-88c2-5a6a-9548-130464947fbb" :answer/type :answer.type/math] [:db/add "9610abe5-88c2-5a6a-9548-130464947fbb" :answer/value "4"] [:db/ensure "9610abe5-88c2-5a6a-9548-130464947fbb" :answer/validate] [:db/add "bd492817-3b4f-5f52-a867-ec13d1736da4" :answer-field/id #uuid "bd492817-3b4f-5f52-a867-ec13d1736da4"] [:db/add "bd492817-3b4f-5f52-a867-ec13d1736da4" :answer-field/key "field-2"] [:db/add "bd492817-3b4f-5f52-a867-ec13d1736da4" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank] [:db/add "bd492817-3b4f-5f52-a867-ec13d1736da4" :answer-field/choices "9610abe5-88c2-5a6a-9548-130464947fbb"] [:db/add "bd492817-3b4f-5f52-a867-ec13d1736da4" :answer-field/correct "9610abe5-88c2-5a6a-9548-130464947fbb"] [:db/ensure "bd492817-3b4f-5f52-a867-ec13d1736da4" :answer-field/validate] [:db/add "f3ed1e68-8185-59c7-af32-90da4c194c8f" :question/id #uuid "f3ed1e68-8185-59c7-af32-90da4c194c8f"] [:db/add "f3ed1e68-8185-59c7-af32-90da4c194c8f" :question/problem "The vectors are drawn on a square grid: $\\overrightarrow{OA}=\\mathbf{a}$, $\\overrightarrow{OB}=\\mathbf{b}$, and $\\overrightarrow{OC}=\\mathbf{c}$.\n\n![Vector diagram](images/bd/bd443698b64001fdc9f2c7b8f1d3fe44bd94ec7d6bf01a953acd5ca80020e1dd.png)\n\nGiven that $\\mathbf{c}=\\lambda\\mathbf{a}+\\mu\\mathbf{b}$, find $\\lambda$ and $\\mu$.\n\n$\\lambda=$ {{field-1}}\n\n$\\mu=$ {{field-2}}"] [:db/add "f3ed1e68-8185-59c7-af32-90da4c194c8f" :question/worked-solution "![Completed vector route](images/18/185ec3520a1b188d114072bf756f6a7e79400509fb9aa696fcfe0211106deaa9.png)\n\nConstruct the route $O\\to X\\to C$, first parallel to $\\mathbf{a}$ and then parallel to $\\mathbf{b}$.\n\nAlong $OX$, move $4$ squares right and $4$ squares up. A copy of $\\mathbf{a}$ moves $2$ squares right and $2$ squares up. Thus $OX=2|\\mathbf{a}|$ and the segment points in the same direction to $\\mathbf{a}$. Hence $\\overrightarrow{OX}=2\\mathbf{a}$.\n\nAlong $XC$, move $4$ squares up. A copy of $\\mathbf{b}$ moves $1$ square up. Thus $XC=4|\\mathbf{b}|$ and the segment points in the same direction to $\\mathbf{b}$. Hence $\\overrightarrow{XC}=4\\mathbf{b}$.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathbf{c}&=\\overrightarrow{OX}+\\overrightarrow{XC}\\\\&=2\\mathbf{a}+4\\mathbf{b}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $\\mathbf{a}$ and $\\mathbf{b}$ are not parallel, their coefficients are unique. Matching coefficients gives $\\lambda=2$ and $\\mu=4$."] [:db/add "f3ed1e68-8185-59c7-af32-90da4c194c8f" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy] [:db/add "f3ed1e68-8185-59c7-af32-90da4c194c8f" :question/answer-fields "e1801d11-b878-56a6-a349-2f7b86d97789"] [:db/add "f3ed1e68-8185-59c7-af32-90da4c194c8f" :question/answer-fields "bd492817-3b4f-5f52-a867-ec13d1736da4"] [:db/ensure "f3ed1e68-8185-59c7-af32-90da4c194c8f" :question/validate] [:db/add 17592186096652 :knowledge-point/questions "f3ed1e68-8185-59c7-af32-90da4c194c8f"] [:db/add "ea0d6f52-b6dc-5398-a420-f2eb2ac0c971" :answer/id #uuid "ea0d6f52-b6dc-5398-a420-f2eb2ac0c971"] [:db/add "ea0d6f52-b6dc-5398-a420-f2eb2ac0c971" :answer/type :answer.type/math] [:db/add "ea0d6f52-b6dc-5398-a420-f2eb2ac0c971" :answer/value "3"] [:db/ensure "ea0d6f52-b6dc-5398-a420-f2eb2ac0c971" :answer/validate] [:db/add "5245cf53-eec4-5f4b-8d6b-7cf7fd927606" :answer-field/id #uuid "5245cf53-eec4-5f4b-8d6b-7cf7fd927606"] [:db/add "5245cf53-eec4-5f4b-8d6b-7cf7fd927606" :answer-field/key "field-1"] [:db/add "5245cf53-eec4-5f4b-8d6b-7cf7fd927606" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank] [:db/add "5245cf53-eec4-5f4b-8d6b-7cf7fd927606" :answer-field/choices "ea0d6f52-b6dc-5398-a420-f2eb2ac0c971"] [:db/add "5245cf53-eec4-5f4b-8d6b-7cf7fd927606" :answer-field/correct "ea0d6f52-b6dc-5398-a420-f2eb2ac0c971"] [:db/ensure "5245cf53-eec4-5f4b-8d6b-7cf7fd927606" :answer-field/validate] [:db/add "414e0c6f-3aba-596b-89b8-d64153bdb716" :answer/id #uuid "414e0c6f-3aba-596b-89b8-d64153bdb716"] [:db/add "414e0c6f-3aba-596b-89b8-d64153bdb716" :answer/type :answer.type/math] [:db/add "414e0c6f-3aba-596b-89b8-d64153bdb716" :answer/value "1"] [:db/ensure "414e0c6f-3aba-596b-89b8-d64153bdb716" :answer/validate] [:db/add "ba3691cf-1ef0-54cd-ada6-23c1a5d67bfb" :answer-field/id #uuid "ba3691cf-1ef0-54cd-ada6-23c1a5d67bfb"] [:db/add "ba3691cf-1ef0-54cd-ada6-23c1a5d67bfb" :answer-field/key "field-2"] [:db/add "ba3691cf-1ef0-54cd-ada6-23c1a5d67bfb" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank] [:db/add "ba3691cf-1ef0-54cd-ada6-23c1a5d67bfb" :answer-field/choices "414e0c6f-3aba-596b-89b8-d64153bdb716"] [:db/add "ba3691cf-1ef0-54cd-ada6-23c1a5d67bfb" :answer-field/correct "414e0c6f-3aba-596b-89b8-d64153bdb716"] [:db/ensure "ba3691cf-1ef0-54cd-ada6-23c1a5d67bfb" :answer-field/validate] [:db/add "4fac9158-dfdb-5b87-889d-9cccc9068bbb" :question/id #uuid "4fac9158-dfdb-5b87-889d-9cccc9068bbb"] [:db/add "4fac9158-dfdb-5b87-889d-9cccc9068bbb" :question/problem "The vectors are drawn on a square grid: $\\overrightarrow{OA}=\\mathbf{a}$, $\\overrightarrow{OB}=\\mathbf{b}$, and $\\overrightarrow{OC}=\\mathbf{c}$.\n\n![Vector diagram](images/26/261d12a56adceb39a06d29e0a39abc6e839909025587c60989d0903bc04d7e9b.png)\n\nGiven that $\\mathbf{c}=\\lambda\\mathbf{a}+\\mu\\mathbf{b}$, find $\\lambda$ and $\\mu$.\n\n$\\lambda=$ {{field-1}}\n\n$\\mu=$ {{field-2}}"] [:db/add "4fac9158-dfdb-5b87-889d-9cccc9068bbb" :question/worked-solution "![Completed vector route](images/37/37cde014f9c3a9e3a654530709ac908b001cdd887709ebb96a957ffe0968f92b.png)\n\nConstruct the route $O\\to X\\to C$, first parallel to $\\mathbf{a}$ and then parallel to $\\mathbf{b}$.\n\nAlong $OX$, move $3$ squares left. A copy of $\\mathbf{a}$ moves $1$ square left. Thus $OX=3|\\mathbf{a}|$ and the segment points in the same direction to $\\mathbf{a}$. Hence $\\overrightarrow{OX}=3\\mathbf{a}$.\n\nAlong $XC$, move $1$ square left and $2$ squares down. A copy of $\\mathbf{b}$ moves $1$ square left and $2$ squares down. Thus $XC=1|\\mathbf{b}|$ and the segment points in the same direction to $\\mathbf{b}$. Hence $\\overrightarrow{XC}=\\mathbf{b}$.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathbf{c}&=\\overrightarrow{OX}+\\overrightarrow{XC}\\\\&=3\\mathbf{a}+\\mathbf{b}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $\\mathbf{a}$ and $\\mathbf{b}$ are not parallel, their coefficients are unique. Matching coefficients gives $\\lambda=3$ and $\\mu=1$."] [:db/add "4fac9158-dfdb-5b87-889d-9cccc9068bbb" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy] [:db/add "4fac9158-dfdb-5b87-889d-9cccc9068bbb" :question/answer-fields "5245cf53-eec4-5f4b-8d6b-7cf7fd927606"] [:db/add "4fac9158-dfdb-5b87-889d-9cccc9068bbb" :question/answer-fields "ba3691cf-1ef0-54cd-ada6-23c1a5d67bfb"] [:db/ensure "4fac9158-dfdb-5b87-889d-9cccc9068bbb" :question/validate] [:db/add 17592186096652 :knowledge-point/questions "4fac9158-dfdb-5b87-889d-9cccc9068bbb"] [:db/add "90c91475-590b-5e00-8285-6299a5d31cda" :answer/id #uuid "90c91475-590b-5e00-8285-6299a5d31cda"] [:db/add "90c91475-590b-5e00-8285-6299a5d31cda" :answer/type :answer.type/math] [:db/add "90c91475-590b-5e00-8285-6299a5d31cda" :answer/value "2"] [:db/ensure "90c91475-590b-5e00-8285-6299a5d31cda" :answer/validate] [:db/add "666898ba-bbe5-5cf0-be09-0c9e47ed24ca" :answer-field/id #uuid "666898ba-bbe5-5cf0-be09-0c9e47ed24ca"] [:db/add "666898ba-bbe5-5cf0-be09-0c9e47ed24ca" :answer-field/key "field-1"] [:db/add "666898ba-bbe5-5cf0-be09-0c9e47ed24ca" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank] [:db/add "666898ba-bbe5-5cf0-be09-0c9e47ed24ca" :answer-field/choices "90c91475-590b-5e00-8285-6299a5d31cda"] [:db/add "666898ba-bbe5-5cf0-be09-0c9e47ed24ca" :answer-field/correct "90c91475-590b-5e00-8285-6299a5d31cda"] [:db/ensure "666898ba-bbe5-5cf0-be09-0c9e47ed24ca" :answer-field/validate] [:db/add "5f98edeb-91ab-5314-aac5-6f201d6c28a7" :answer/id #uuid "5f98edeb-91ab-5314-aac5-6f201d6c28a7"] [:db/add "5f98edeb-91ab-5314-aac5-6f201d6c28a7" :answer/type :answer.type/math] [:db/add "5f98edeb-91ab-5314-aac5-6f201d6c28a7" :answer/value "4"] [:db/ensure "5f98edeb-91ab-5314-aac5-6f201d6c28a7" :answer/validate] [:db/add "d3a941ed-e775-596b-870f-23d6b124cb3b" :answer-field/id #uuid "d3a941ed-e775-596b-870f-23d6b124cb3b"] [:db/add "d3a941ed-e775-596b-870f-23d6b124cb3b" :answer-field/key "field-2"] [:db/add "d3a941ed-e775-596b-870f-23d6b124cb3b" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank] [:db/add "d3a941ed-e775-596b-870f-23d6b124cb3b" :answer-field/choices "5f98edeb-91ab-5314-aac5-6f201d6c28a7"] [:db/add "d3a941ed-e775-596b-870f-23d6b124cb3b" :answer-field/correct "5f98edeb-91ab-5314-aac5-6f201d6c28a7"] [:db/ensure "d3a941ed-e775-596b-870f-23d6b124cb3b" :answer-field/validate] [:db/add "10155d1b-0d1c-5dfa-a752-9c65ac5d600c" :question/id #uuid "10155d1b-0d1c-5dfa-a752-9c65ac5d600c"] [:db/add "10155d1b-0d1c-5dfa-a752-9c65ac5d600c" :question/problem "The vectors are drawn on a square grid: $\\overrightarrow{OA}=\\mathbf{a}$, $\\overrightarrow{OB}=\\mathbf{b}$, and $\\overrightarrow{OC}=\\mathbf{c}$.\n\n![Vector diagram](images/00/0017e5d7fc8701f0a038ef80a8c8bce552f568dd5708aae29b28e050e74d3591.png)\n\nGiven that $\\mathbf{c}=\\lambda\\mathbf{a}+\\mu\\mathbf{b}$, find $\\lambda$ and $\\mu$.\n\n$\\lambda=$ {{field-1}}\n\n$\\mu=$ {{field-2}}"] [:db/add "10155d1b-0d1c-5dfa-a752-9c65ac5d600c" :question/worked-solution "![Completed vector route](images/a6/a6a7400a3b0aafed09994ce692174418fae00d0e56aade003e7ac77d7c922ca1.png)\n\nConstruct the route $O\\to X\\to C$, first parallel to $\\mathbf{b}$ and then parallel to $\\mathbf{a}$.\n\nAlong $OX$, move $8$ squares up. A copy of $\\mathbf{b}$ moves $2$ squares up. Thus $OX=4|\\mathbf{b}|$ and the segment points in the same direction to $\\mathbf{b}$. Hence $\\overrightarrow{OX}=4\\mathbf{b}$.\n\nAlong $XC$, move $2$ squares left and $2$ squares up. A copy of $\\mathbf{a}$ moves $1$ square left and $1$ square up. Thus $XC=2|\\mathbf{a}|$ and the segment points in the same direction to $\\mathbf{a}$. Hence $\\overrightarrow{XC}=2\\mathbf{a}$.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathbf{c}&=\\overrightarrow{OX}+\\overrightarrow{XC}\\\\&=4\\mathbf{b}+2\\mathbf{a}\\\\&=2\\mathbf{a}+4\\mathbf{b}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nReorder the terms to match their vector names. Since $\\mathbf{a}$ and $\\mathbf{b}$ are not parallel, their coefficients are unique. Matching coefficients gives $\\lambda=2$ and $\\mu=4$."] [:db/add "10155d1b-0d1c-5dfa-a752-9c65ac5d600c" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy] [:db/add "10155d1b-0d1c-5dfa-a752-9c65ac5d600c" :question/answer-fields "666898ba-bbe5-5cf0-be09-0c9e47ed24ca"] [:db/add "10155d1b-0d1c-5dfa-a752-9c65ac5d600c" :question/answer-fields "d3a941ed-e775-596b-870f-23d6b124cb3b"] [:db/ensure "10155d1b-0d1c-5dfa-a752-9c65ac5d600c" :question/validate] [:db/add 17592186096652 :knowledge-point/questions "10155d1b-0d1c-5dfa-a752-9c65ac5d600c"] [:db/add "652ceceb-b89c-58fa-b198-38de91333cd4" :answer/id #uuid "652ceceb-b89c-58fa-b198-38de91333cd4"] [:db/add "652ceceb-b89c-58fa-b198-38de91333cd4" :answer/type :answer.type/math] [:db/add "652ceceb-b89c-58fa-b198-38de91333cd4" :answer/value "2"] [:db/ensure "652ceceb-b89c-58fa-b198-38de91333cd4" :